{
  "info": {
    "name": "Week 3 - Task Manager API (mini project)",
    "description": "SkillNexis Week 3 mini project. The React client at http://localhost:5175 calls exactly these routes.\n\nRun 'Register user A' first: it saves the JWT into {{token}}, and every /api/tasks request sends it. The three 'Create' requests set up the data the filter requests expect, so run the collection top to bottom.\n\n'Upload an avatar' is multipart/form-data - Postman cannot store a file inside a collection, so open that request, go to Body > form-data and pick an image for the 'avatar' key.\n\nThe folder 'Second user - proof tasks are private' registers a different account and tries to touch user A's task. Every one of those is 404: a task can only be reached by the account that owns it, and a 403 would confirm it exists.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5005"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "taskId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "otherToken",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
